{"entity":"story","version":1,"id":"graph-model-and-assertions","revision":1,"type":"aep.entity.create/v1","from_state":null,"to_state":"draft","changed":{"body":"## Context\n\nDesign § 13–14 make the assertion the fundamental primitive, with valid time and transaction time\nas separate ranges; § 17 and § 36 give its validation and status states; § 21–23 give the canonical\nand transient graphs and ask that a `Canonical → Transient` reference be impossible to represent;\n§ 34 gives the revision root; § 47 gives the query scopes a reader chooses between. This story is\nthe data model of the graph. It has no writer: mutation arrives in the next two stories.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nA compile-fail test shows that `CanonicalGraph` cannot hold a `TransientRef`, and over the § 65\nfixture (Alice `CEO_OF` Acme until 2026-03-12, Bob from then) the active query returns Bob, the\n`valid_at(2025-06-01)` query returns Alice, and neither returns a `Retracted` or `Superseded`\nassertion.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `crates/ekr-graph/src/node.rs`, `edge.rs` — `Node` (with `type_state` from amendment 87),\n  `Edge` (`systems/ekr/domains/graph.yaml`)\n- `crates/ekr-graph/src/assertion.rs` — `Assertion`, `Subject`, `Predicate`, `Object`,\n  `TemporalRange`, `ValidationState`, `AssertionStatus`\n- `crates/ekr-graph/src/evidence.rs` — `Evidence`, `EvidenceSource`, `Observation`,\n  `ObservationContent` (including `Blob`, amendment 86), `Support`\n- `crates/ekr-graph/src/root.rs` — `GraphRoot`, `Root` (the revision root of design § 34)\n- `crates/ekr-graph/src/canonical.rs`, `transient.rs` — `CanonicalGraph`, `TransientGraph`,\n  `CanonicalRef<T>`, `TransientRef<T>` (design § 23)\n- `crates/ekr-graph/src/snapshot.rs` — `GraphSnapshot`, `QueryScope` (design § 47: active,\n  as-of revision, valid-at time, include disputed)\n- `crates/ekr-graph/src/lib.rs`\n- `crates/ekr-graph/tests/compile_fail/` (trybuild)\n\n## Notes\n\nDepends on `story:ontology-types-and-values`. `TransientGraph` exists so the membrane is typed\nfrom the start; the incubation forest that uses it is P3. `KnowledgeState` (design § 29) is a\nfield on `GraphRoot` here and gains its commands in P3.\n","title":"Graph model: nodes, edges, bitemporal assertions, evidence, the canonical/transient membrane"},"args":{"command":"create-entity","data":{"body":"## Context\n\nDesign § 13–14 make the assertion the fundamental primitive, with valid time and transaction time\nas separate ranges; § 17 and § 36 give its validation and status states; § 21–23 give the canonical\nand transient graphs and ask that a `Canonical → Transient` reference be impossible to represent;\n§ 34 gives the revision root; § 47 gives the query scopes a reader chooses between. This story is\nthe data model of the graph. It has no writer: mutation arrives in the next two stories.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nA compile-fail test shows that `CanonicalGraph` cannot hold a `TransientRef`, and over the § 65\nfixture (Alice `CEO_OF` Acme until 2026-03-12, Bob from then) the active query returns Bob, the\n`valid_at(2025-06-01)` query returns Alice, and neither returns a `Retracted` or `Superseded`\nassertion.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `crates/ekr-graph/src/node.rs`, `edge.rs` — `Node` (with `type_state` from amendment 87),\n  `Edge` (`systems/ekr/domains/graph.yaml`)\n- `crates/ekr-graph/src/assertion.rs` — `Assertion`, `Subject`, `Predicate`, `Object`,\n  `TemporalRange`, `ValidationState`, `AssertionStatus`\n- `crates/ekr-graph/src/evidence.rs` — `Evidence`, `EvidenceSource`, `Observation`,\n  `ObservationContent` (including `Blob`, amendment 86), `Support`\n- `crates/ekr-graph/src/root.rs` — `GraphRoot`, `Root` (the revision root of design § 34)\n- `crates/ekr-graph/src/canonical.rs`, `transient.rs` — `CanonicalGraph`, `TransientGraph`,\n  `CanonicalRef<T>`, `TransientRef<T>` (design § 23)\n- `crates/ekr-graph/src/snapshot.rs` — `GraphSnapshot`, `QueryScope` (design § 47: active,\n  as-of revision, valid-at time, include disputed)\n- `crates/ekr-graph/src/l